{55}{And good day to you.... Sir.}{And good day to you.... Madam.}{}{}{0}{re -10}
{56}{}{}{}{}{}{}
{57}{I see you don't know about tanglewood. It's an extremely wet wood but quite hard at the same time. You can't get that stuff to burn unless it's dried for three years or more and even then, it burns very slowly. That's why they make pipe bowls out of the burls. And then there's the fact that the entire grove been suckin' up all that extra water that's been flowin' around the island. All the kerosene in world wouldn't burn those trees.}{I see you don't know about tanglewood. It's an extremely wet wood but quite hard at the same time. You can't get that stuff to burn unless it's dried for three years or more and even then, it burns very slowly. That's why they make pipe bowls out of the burls. And then there's the fact that the entire grove been suckin' up all that extra water that's been flowin' around the island. All the kerosene in world wouldn't burn those trees.}{}{}{}{}
{58}{Of course. You mentioned the spiders were contained.  [You motion towards the banana grove] What about the ones over there?}{}{5}{}{65}{}
{59}{Uhhh.... [You motion towards the banana grove] You said spiders were con-tained. Whut about dose ones?}{}{-4}{}{65}{}
{60}{I see. Well, this has been an interesting conversation, but I don't see where it concerns me, so I shall bid you good day.}{}{5}{}{55}{}
{61}{Well, dis been intrustin' but not matter to me. Me say bye now and hope your help come soon.}{}{-4}{}{55}{}

{65}{Oh those are just blackies. They're dangerous, but they eat the birds and such that would damage the crops. We leave 'em alone until it's harvest or fertilize time, then we light off the smudge pots and toss a few tanglewood leaves in the fire. The smoke chases them out of the grove and we can work in safety. Any of them that tries to come across the road gets a torch shoved at him.}{Oh those are just blackies. They're dangerous, but they eat the birds and such that would damage the crops. We leave 'em alone until it's harvest or fertilize time, then we light off the smudge pots and toss a few tanglewood leaves in the fire. The smoke chases them out of the grove and we can work in safety. Any of them that tries to come across the road gets a torch shoved at him.}{}{}{}{}
{66}{I see. Well, you folks certainly do have a problem. Perhaps I may be of assistance. Who would I talk to about lending my services?}{}{5}{}{75}{}
{67}{Is good. Yuh... Well, you pee-pul do have a problum. Maybe me can help. Who do I talk to?}{}{-4}{}{75}{}
